window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201","paragraphs":["Returning the Favor (1)","I didn’t understand.","No matter how many times I thought it over, I simply couldn’t understand.","I had clearly heard that dragons treasured their young above all else.","In other words, they would never entrust their children to someone they didn’t trust.","If anything happened to the hatchling while it was here, I would face terrifying retaliation.","Moreover, this was the Forest of Four Seasons. Unless animals belonged to the same group, they were essentially enemies.","There was the kangaroo arena, which functioned as neutral territory, but that was an extremely rare exception founded upon an unspoken agreement.","The moment they left the neutral zone, they became enemies again. In other words, nowhere was truly safe.","\"Pibiiii~\"","\"Kyuuu~ Kyu~\"","So why had the dragon entrusted its hatchling to me?","The hatchling was currently running around and playing excitedly with Wonmo.","Whenever the hatchling took flight with a flap of its wings, Wonmo hopped up and down after it.","Watching the two adorable babies play together put my mind at ease, but that feeling didn’t last long.","\"Mister.\"","\"....\"","\"This is your first time seeing anything like this too, right? It’s my first time as well.\"","I had absolutely no idea how I was supposed to treat the hatchling.","Had the dragon genuinely mistaken this place for a daycare center and left its child with me, or was there some other reason?","Whatever the case, one thing was certain.","I had to protect the hatchling at all costs.","Only yesterday, it had crawled into the cave with wounds covering its entire body.","I didn’t know what had attacked it, but there was a high chance that threat was still nearby.","The dragon probably went to slaughter whatever did it.","Perhaps it had only entrusted the hatchling to me until that was done.","I released a long sigh and accepted reality.","I couldn’t drive the hatchling away, so we had no choice but to get along.","Fortunately, the hatchling seemed to like this place and played well with Wonmo.","\"Kyuuuuu~\"","\"Piiii~\"","Even now, they were using Largo’s neck as a slide.","Largo himself was sweating profusely as he nervously watched the hatchling’s every move.","Maybe this actually makes the shelter safer?","Dragons were terrifying.","And that fear seemed deeply engraved not only into humanity, but into all animals.","Just as Largo was doing now, most animals wouldn’t even consider laying a paw on the hatchling.","If so, the shelter might benefit from the same deterrent effect.","Of course, since this was the Forest of Four Seasons, there was no telling what sort of monstrous creature might appear.","It’s basically a living nuclear bomb.","That was genuinely how dragons were treated.","All-Father had once told me that a dragon heart alone possessed enough power to annihilate an entire city.","If even its heart held that much power, what about the creature carrying that heart?","There was no need to ask.","I silently watched the hatchling and Wonmo playing before accessing the Gallery.","I wanted to inform everyone about the current situation and, while I was at it, ask why the dragon might have left its hatchling with me.","Title: I opened a daycare center","Wild Grylls","(A photo of the hatchling playing with Wonmo)","(A video of the hatchling running around excitedly)","(A video of the hatchling struggling to drag Wonmo)","I don’t know why, but the dragon left its hatchling with me.","Does anyone know the reason? They originally left together, but then the dragon came back and dropped the hatchling off.","I thought dragons treasured their young. Does anyone know why it’s doing this?","└ Heavenly Demon: If it was willing to leave its young with you, it must trust you. In a way, that is only natural.","└ Wild Grylls: Why would it trust me?","└ Heavenly Demon: Did you not say dragons were as intelligent as humans? Moreover, unlike humans, beasts do not forget kindness or grudges.","└ Wild Grylls: Dumping a hatchling on me isn’t repaying a favor. It’s throwing a bomb at me;;","└ SwordMaster: Don’t look at it so negatively. In a sense, this means you have a dragon’s protection, doesn’t it?","└ A person under a dragon’s protection. Didn’t that appear in legends too?","└ Yeah, but that came from mythology. Those stories originated from when dragons ruled over humanity.","└ So the gods killed those dragons and liberated humanity?","└ That’s also true.","└ Why, though? To a kingdom protected by a dragon, wouldn’t the gods have seemed like invaders?","└ Starlight Princess: Because the dragons’ exploitation was so severe. That’s also where the legends about dragon lairs containing all manner of treasures originated.","└ Sounds like dragons had really shitty personalities, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: They weren’t particularly pleasant. There are even stories of them killing people with their breath whenever something displeased them. That dragon is relatively good-natured by comparison.","└ Aren’t you basically living on borrowed time, then?","└ Not even that. His life is hanging by a thread.","└ A thread hanging from another thread, lmaooo.","└ Starlight Princess: You people are truly awful.","Most of them had reached the same conclusion as me.","Since I had protected its child, the dragon had judged this to be a safe place.","The problem was that dragons were generally ferocious by nature, so there was no telling when it might suddenly turn on me.","One way or another, it remained a ticking time bomb.","Ugh. I don’t know anymore.","I might as well eat. Worrying about it wouldn’t solve anything.","I would have to become as close to the hatchling as possible, making the dragon less willing to hurt me.","Before that, I decided to give it a name.","I couldn’t keep calling it \"the hatchling\" every time.","If I ask the Gallery, they’ll only suggest all kinds of ridiculous names.","From now on, I would choose the names myself.","As it happened, a suitable name had already come to mind.","A species that had once conquered Earth before going extinct after a great cataclysm.","And the most famous name associated with that species.","Recalling that name, I approached the hatchling.","Then I lifted the hatchling, which had been playing excitedly with Wonmo, and spoke.","\"Tyranno.\"","\"Pii?\"","\"Your name is Tyranno now. Got it?\"","\"Pii!\"","Now that I had named it, it was time to put it down.","It would take some time for it to recognize its own name, but that was fine.","I was about to start preparing our meal when—","\"...Tyranno?\"","Ludwig asked with a slightly bewildered expression.","He apparently hadn’t imagined that I would go so far as to name it.","\"Yes. We’ll probably be seeing a lot of it from now on, so it needs a name.\"","Ludwig nodded silently.","I was the owner of this place, so he seemed to respect my decision.","\"I’m going upriver for now. Please stay here.\"","Carrying Fast Sloth on my back, I headed upriver and left Ludwig at the shelter.","Someone of Ludwig’s strength would be more than capable of defending it, and Kkobong was there too.","\"By the way, weren’t you afraid of the dragon?\"","I asked Fast Sloth as we made our way upstream.","Everyone else had been terrified by the dragon, but Fast Sloth had leisurely scratched his back.","I couldn’t tell whether he was brave or simply incapable of feeling fear.","Naturally, Fast Sloth didn’t answer me. As always, his expression remained relaxed.","I wished he could speak like the gorillas.","Did he even have vocal cords in the first place? Still, at least he could understand me, so it was fine.","Roooooar!","Perhaps because the rain had stopped some time ago, the river had returned to its normal level.","There weren’t any fish lying scattered around the riverbank either. The animals had probably carried them away.","I had originally planned to come upriver first thing in the morning, but the dragon’s sudden appearance had made that impossible.","I’ll just set the fish traps.","It hadn’t rained heavily yesterday, so there was no need to erect any stone barriers.","I quickly set the traps and returned to the shelter.","When I arrived, I was greeted by an amusing sight.","\"Chirp! Chirp! Chirp!\"","\"Chirp! Chirp!\"","While I was upriver, Ludwig seemed to have planted wheat seeds in the field.","The wheat soon began growing at a tremendous rate, naturally attracting a flock of birds.","Under normal circumstances, they would have stripped the entire field bare.","\"Piiiiik!\"","\"Chiiiiirp!\"","\"Chirp, chirp, chirp!\"","Flap-flap-flap!","But the instant Tyranno roared, the entire flock fled in a panic.","Despite being only a baby, he apparently possessed the natural intimidation of a dragon.","Thanks to him, Ludwig harvested the wheat without suffering any interference.","\"Oh?\"","That was unexpected.","If this continued, harvesting wheat would become much easier from now on.","Ludwig must have reached the same conclusion, because he looked at Tyranno with a peculiar expression.","Tyranno paid him no attention and immediately became absorbed in playing with Wonmo again.","\"Come on, you two. Eat before you go back to playing.\"","First, we needed to eat.","As I had mentioned before, we still had some fish left.","The problem was that Tyranno could easily devour an entire fish by himself.","There were five of us: me, Ludwig, Wonmo, Kkobong, and Tyranno.","We consumed five whole fish with every meal.","Fortunately, Largo only ate grass. Otherwise, the situation would have been horrifying.","I’ll either have to install more traps or expand the fields.","There was something else that concerned me.","Would Wonmo and Tyranno become picky eaters?","Wonmo was a bear and therefore omnivorous, but Tyranno was most likely a carnivore.","Unless Tyranno’s mother started delivering meat to us, I would have to ration our food for the time being.","Plump—","Once we had finished eating, I noticed a slight change in Wonmo.","He had visibly put on weight.","It wasn’t just his stomach that had become rounder; his overall size had increased.","That probably meant winter would arrive soon.","We had already prepared for it, but what would happen to Tyranno?","Would his mother take him away herself, or would she continue leaving him here?","\"Kyuuuuu.\"","Now that his belly was full, Wonmo toddled into the cave for a nap.","Tyranno blocked his path, apparently wanting to continue playing, but the difference in their sizes was too great.","Even when Tyranno blocked him with his body and tried pulling him back with his mouth, Wonmo didn’t budge.","\"Piiiiing....\"","When Wonmo eventually settled down for his nap, Tyranno looked heartbroken.","As if asking why Wonmo was sleeping when they could still play, he repeatedly pressed down on him with his forepaws.","But Wonmo had already departed for dreamland.","There was no waking him now.","Doesn’t this one sleep?","As far as I knew, most baby animals spent more than half the day asleep.","Dragons must have been an exception, because Tyranno was still brimming with energy.","I watched the dejected Tyranno before casually asking,","\"Tyranno, do you want to play with me?\"","\"Pii?\"","Flap! Flap!","Did he understand human speech too?","The moment I spoke to him, he began flapping his tiny wings.","Even his large eyes sparkled with excitement. Apparently, he was desperate to play.","Come to think of it, don’t dragons like shiny things?","I asked Tyranno to wait for a moment and opened a box.","Inside was the mithril left over from the incident involving Ludwig’s prosthetic leg.","Mithril was a material that glowed green, so perhaps Tyranno would like it.","I’ll roll it around for him to chase.","I took out a fist-sized piece of mithril shaped like a ball.","When I showed it to Tyranno, his expression immediately filled with curiosity.","Just as expected, dragons loved shiny things—","\"Chomp!\"","\"...?\"","Crunch! Crack! Crunch!","—though perhaps he loved them in a different sense.","Tyranno swallowed the mithril in one bite and chewed it with great relish.","Mithril was renowned for being as hard as steel, yet he was eating it like a cracker.","Gulp!","\"Piiii~\"","\"Was it tasty?\"","\"Pii!\"","As long as he enjoyed it, I supposed it was fine.","***","Dragons were widely known as the strongest living creatures on earth.","They possessed immense strength born from their overwhelming size.","They had minds intelligent enough to wield magic like humans.","They had wings that allowed them to soar freely through the sky.","Finally, they possessed breath attacks capable of melting everything in their path.","Very few beings could fight such creatures on equal footing.","That was why humans and most animals feared incurring a dragon’s wrath.","Most creatures ignored hatchlings as though they didn’t even exist. If anyone harmed one, that individual would be exiled from their group.","Expelling one member was preferable to having the entire group annihilated for the offense.","But that only applied outside the Forest of Four Seasons.","The Forest of Four Seasons was home to monsters every bit as terrifying as dragons.","There were already creatures that seemed to belong in a kaiju film, like the giant crab and giant crayfish Grylls had encountered at the lake.","In other words, monsters comparable to dragons in both size and strength existed here.","\"Grrrrrr.\"","The gray dragon released a terrifying growl as it glared ahead.","Its expression was murderous, as though it intended to tear apart the creature before it at any moment.","The dragon was currently inside none other than its own lair—its home.","Under normal circumstances, it would have rested there, but something prevented it from doing so.","Rustle—","An enormous white serpent had brazenly occupied the lair.","It radiated a different kind of oppressive presence from the dragon, while its flickering tongue seemed to be taunting its opponent.","The monster was more than twice the dragon’s length.","Its bulk was equally astounding. If it opened its jaws wide, it looked capable of swallowing the dragon whole.","It wasn’t one of the imoogi commonly found in the Central Plains.","It appeared to be a far superior creature.","\"Shaaaaa...!\"","When the enormous white serpent opened its mouth, a pair of razor-sharp venomous fangs came into view.","Purple liquid dripped from them toward the ground.","Sssssss!","No—it didn’t seep into the ground.","Even solid rock melted the instant the venom touched it.","This monster was the reason the dragon had been forced to leave its hatchling unattended.","It was also the reason the dragon had no choice but to entrust its hatchling to Grylls for a time.","Like the sky whale, it was a monstrous creature that should only have existed during the Mythological Age.","\"Graaaaaaaaah!\"","\"Shaaaaaaaaa!\"","In one corner of the Forest of Four Seasons, a life-or-death struggle began."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202","paragraphs":["Returning the Favor (2)","The sight of a dragon effortlessly chewing through mithril made me wonder whether an accident might happen soon.","Tyranno might think he was biting gently, only to tear off chunks of flesh.","The risk was especially high because Tyranno often played with Wonmo.","Fortunately, Wonmo had already learned to control his strength while playing with the raccoons.","For both their sakes, Tyranno needed to learn the same lesson.","\"Tyranno, bite me here.\"","\"Bebi?\"","With Tyranno perched on my shoulder, I pointed at my forearm.","He closely examined the spot I was pointing at, seemingly focused.","\"Bite down slowly until I say it hurts. Like this. Chomp!\"","When I mimed biting my forearm, Tyranno tilted his head.","Rather than explaining it verbally, I decided to demonstrate.","It was fine if he wanted to nibble us as a sign of affection, but his bite was far too powerful.","He needed to learn how to bite gently before an accident occurred.","In other words, I needed to teach him restraint and drill it into him.","\"Pii!\"","Tyranno apparently understood what I meant, because he smiled brightly and bit my forearm.","Crunch!","\"Aaaaaaargh! No! No, that’s not it! Let go! Let go!\"","\"Pipi?!\"","The moment he bit down, my bone nearly snapped.","I hurriedly stopped Tyranno, and he immediately pulled away upon hearing my scream.","When I examined my forearm, I found a distinct set of teeth marks.","How did it leave only marks? It wouldn’t have been strange if his teeth had pierced straight through.","My bone hadn’t broken, but the area was badly bruised.","I would probably have to inject some elixir into it soon.","\"See? Your bite is that strong. You mustn’t bite your friends so hard.\"","\"Piiii....\"","\"It’s okay. It’s okay. Mistakes happen. Come on, let’s try again.\"","Through consistent repetition, Tyranno quickly learned how to control his strength.","His intelligence was so high that he seemed to grasp exactly what I wanted.","Now that I no longer needed to worry about any accidents, only one concern remained.","How am I going to manage our food?","With another mouth to feed, our food shortage had become an urgent problem.","Largo could survive on leaves, but the other animals couldn’t.","Every last one of them is a glutton.","To make matters worse, winter was just around the corner.","I needed to stockpile enough food to survive it.","Potatoes were one of the most obvious foods to store for winter.","GrowGrowGrow had given me seed potatoes, so I only needed to plant them.","...Should I make kimchi too?","The pointless thought crossed my mind, but I immediately dismissed it.","Who had time to make kimchi in a situation like this? I didn’t even eat much kimchi to begin with.","It seemed best to search through the Gallery.","If I couldn’t find the answer, I could always ask someone.","Oh... Bread is an option too.","I quickly found several foods suitable for winter storage.","There was the smoked meat I had previously made by salting it, as well as salted vegetables.","Rice and wheat were said to be particularly suitable for surviving winter. Both simply needed to be stored somewhere cool.","For now, I planned to ask GrowGrowGrow for help.","If they didn’t have any, I would have to search the auction house for seeds.","There are also cabbages, spinach, radishes, and potatoes, but....","Trying to store too many different foods might only make things confusing.","Let’s survive this winter on wheat, potatoes, and sweet potatoes. In that case....","I needed to learn how to harvest wheat.","Rather than searching for the information myself, I asked GrowGrowGrow. That seemed much faster.","GrowGrowGrow: Once you’ve harvested the wheat, you need to dry it within four hours. Otherwise, its quality will deteriorate.","Wild Grylls: What happens if I don’t?","GrowGrowGrow: It’ll either rot or grow mold, won’t it?","Wild Grylls: ;;","I had originally planned to make bread from wheat flour.","However, after hearing the explanation, I gave up.","There was simply far too much work involved. Noodles would be much easier than bread.","Even producing the flour itself took a long time.","Come to think of it, bakers exist, but there isn’t a profession dedicated solely to cooking rice.","Since I had cooked rice at home every day, I had assumed making bread would be just as manageable.","But just as turning rice into rice cakes was difficult, baking bread was no simple task either.","So I changed my plan from wheat to rice.","GrowGrowGrow didn’t have any rice seeds, so I planned to ask someone else.","I can ask the Heavenly Demon, right?","Since the Central Plains came from a martial-arts world, there was a high chance that rice was available there.","I handed some soil over to GrowGrowGrow and contacted the Heavenly Demon.","Heavenly Demon: You are asking this one for rice?","Wild Grylls: Rice seeds, to be precise. I’m planning to grow it myself.","Heavenly Demon: Very well. This one shall have a close aide procure some for you.","Wild Grylls: Thank you.","Now that I would soon receive rice seeds from the Heavenly Demon, I decided to dry the wheat first.","I needed to thresh it before drying it, but removing every grain by hand would be incredibly difficult.","Therefore, I needed a threshing tool.","Since I would soon be harvesting rice as well, it wasn’t optional but essential.","A threshing tool is one thing, but I’ll also have to remove the husks.... Did farmers really do all this work by hand?","My respect for farmers suddenly began soaring.","I searched the auction house for threshing and husking tools.","\"Isn’t this a comb?\"","I found a threshing tool that looked somewhat like a comb.","More precisely, it was a comb-shaped piece of iron.","I purchased it and examined its construction. It was roughly the size of a person’s head.","I insert the heads of the grain between these teeth and pull, right?","One look was enough to understand how it worked.","So, what should I do next?","Make Ludwig do it, of course.","Before that, I spread a cloth over the ground.","Then I placed a chair at its edge and secured the threshing tool on top of it.","\"Come on. Let’s get to work.\"","\"Mm.\"","Rattle-rattle-rattle!","We inserted the wheat heads between the densely packed teeth and pulled.","Plump, appetizing grains showered onto the cloth.","Lick. Lick.","\"Hey, Tyranno! You can’t eat that!\"","\"Pii?\"","Tyranno tried licking up a few grains in the middle of our work, but I barely managed to stop him.","Afterward, we diligently threshed all the wheat we had harvested so far.","We gathered the separated grains and placed them somewhere that received plenty of sunlight.","Drying them like chili peppers should work.","I didn’t forget to apply insect repellent either.","The birds... won’t come back, right?","The birds had fled from Tyranno’s intimidating presence long ago.","At least while Tyranno was here, they probably wouldn’t return.","So, what should I do while waiting for the grain to dry?","\"Ludwig, I’m going out to scout the area.\"","\"Mm.\"","I headed out to hunt while conducting reconnaissance.","Ludwig should be more than capable of defending the shelter.","Besides, Kkobong was there with him.","Kkobong was also diligently using the threshing tool.","After all, we couldn’t survive the entire winter on nothing but rice and noodles.","I had originally intended to leave Tyranno behind as well.","\"Piiii! Piiii!\"","\"I told you, I’ll only be gone for a little while.\"","\"Piiii! Piiiiii!\"","But he clung to me, demanding that I stay—or take him with me if I insisted on leaving.","He was ridiculously strong.","Left with no choice, I decided to bring Tyranno along on the scouting trip.","Fast Sloth was already clinging to my back.","\"Do you really have to sit there?\"","\"Pii!\"","\"Fine. Do whatever you want.\"","Tyranno settled on top of my head as though it were a nest.","He was slightly heavy, but it wasn’t uncomfortable. It was better than letting him wander around and get lost.","Moreover, bringing him along produced an unexpected benefit: his reactions.","\"Pii.\"","Tyranno raised his head and cried softly, as though sensing something in a particular direction.","I was slightly skeptical, but I headed where he wanted me to go.","\"Oink.\"","\"Oh...?\"","There was a wild boar.","A wild boar comparable in size to a bus.","Its enormous, movie-monster-like body and sharply protruding tusks were particularly striking.","...I saw something like that in the military once, didn’t I?","The memory remained vivid even now.","A wild boar had wandered over while we were working.","There had been a jeep right next to it, yet that miraculous boar had somehow made the vehicle look small.","\"Oiiiiink!\"","A boar far larger than that one charged at me.","I had more or less expected this, so I was about to calmly move out of the way when—","\"Piaaaaaak!\"","Tyranno released an adorable roar from atop my head.","It had worked on the birds, but I wondered whether it would work on a wild boar.","\"Oink?!\"","Screeeeech!","It worked.","Extremely well, in fact.","The moment the boar heard Tyranno’s roar, its eyes widened and it slammed on the brakes.","I didn’t know whether it had recognized him as a hatchling or whether the fear of dragons was simply engraved into its instincts.","One thing was certain: a tremendous opportunity had presented itself.","Seizing the moment, I charged at the boar.","Crunch!","The Heavenly Demon’s sword sank directly into the boar’s forehead.","With its brain reduced to mush, the boar convulsed for a while before collapsing limply.","Thud!","Its body was so enormous that the ground trembled slightly when it fell.","I released the breath I had been holding and stared at the fallen boar.","It was so massive that this one carcass might be enough to last us through the winter.","Of course, I would need to build a large storage room.","Fortunately, I had plenty of ice.","\"...You’re incredible, aren’t you?\"","\"Pii!\"","When I stroked his chin and praised him, Tyranno proudly raised his head.","He seemed to be boasting, See how amazing I am!","It was still adorable, though.","I tightly bound the boar with the rope I had prepared.","There was no way I could carry something this large, so I planned to drag it back.","Still... this is pretty heavy.","That was inevitable, considering its size.","I just had to think of it as our winter food supply.","Just in case, I placed Tyranno on top of the boar and had him keep watch in every direction.","There were far too many thieves in the Forest of Four Seasons to do otherwise.","\"Kyu?\"","When I returned while dragging the boar, Wonmo greeted us after waking from his nap.","Ludwig and Kkobong were still threshing the wheat.","Despite having left only a short while ago, I had returned with an enormous haul.","\"Mister! You know how to butcher animals too, right?\"","\"#%$#\"","\"Then please help me.\"","Butchering this thing alone would take far too long.","Considering its sheer size, I wasn’t even sure I could butcher it properly.","Fortunately, Ludwig appeared quite skilled at it.","Perhaps his countless missions had often forced him to survive on his own.","\"One, two! Pull!\"","\"Hup!\"","\"Gwoong.\"","Despite preparing ourselves, even the preliminary work was difficult.","It reminded me of the saber-toothed tiger.","Butchering normally began by hanging the carcass upside down, which made it easier to drain the blood.","The problem was that the boar was so enormous that even suspending it upside down was difficult.","We enlisted Largo’s help.","He was remarkably strong and managed to hoist the boar to the desired height.","He was essentially a living crane.","I had never expected to use him this way, though.","Trickle, trickle—","Draining all the blood would take some time, so I began constructing a storage room while we waited.","It wasn’t a traditional icehouse, but something closer to a freezer.","It wouldn’t be used to store tools or miscellaneous supplies. It was exclusively for food.","My ability allowed me to produce a nearly unlimited supply of ice, so sufficient insulation would be enough.","I need to make sure the heat can escape properly... Wait, I’m short on sand again?","Whenever I obtained one thing, I discovered that I needed another. Then, once I acquired that, something else would be missing.","It felt as though I had fallen into an endless cycle.","Still, this was only natural.","It might have been different if I lived alone, but as our numbers increased, so did the number of things we needed.","I have enough time. Still, I should hurry.","I traveled downstream to gather sand, returned, and continued building the storage room.","After thoroughly coating the interior with soil and straw for insulation, I resumed butchering the boar.","I wanted to make Kkobong do it, but unfortunately, he was a gorilla.","The structure of his hands made them poorly suited to delicate work like butchering.","Crackle!","Once we had made sufficient progress with the butchering, I placed ice inside the storage room.","After filling it with ice, we stored the butchered boar, grain, vegetables, and everything else that could serve as food.","I’ll cover the entrance with cloth for now. I don’t have enough time to install a proper door.","By the time we finished everything, it was four thirty in the afternoon.","If I had worked alone, I wouldn’t have finished today.","An extra pair of hands truly made an enormous difference.","\"Good work. Would you like to wash up?\"","\"Mm.\"","I prepared bathwater for Ludwig, who had worked harder than anyone else today.","For the record, I planned to wash all the animals, including Kkobong.","Surprisingly, Kkobong was perfectly capable of washing himself. As long as I prepared his bathwater, he took care of everything on his own.","Largo only needed to be brushed and wiped down with a damp cloth.","Finally, there was Tyranno.","\"Piiii! Piiii!\"","\"What’s wrong? You don’t want a bath?\"","\"Piiii! Pii! Piiii!\"","As if he really were a cat, he vehemently refused to wash.","But for the sake of cleanliness, there was no helping it.","I had to bathe him.","He might not have fur, but there was no telling what kind of ticks might be hiding on his body.","\"You won’t get dinner if you don’t take a bath.\"","\"...Piiiing.\"","Fortunately, the threat of withholding food made him obedient.","And so, another uneventful day came to an end."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203","paragraphs":["Returning the Favor (3)","While Tyranno was settling in well at Grylls’s shelter—","Boooom! Bang!","The dragon had been locked in a life-or-death struggle with the enormous white serpent all day long.","The giant white serpent was every bit as formidable as its size and imposing presence suggested.","Its maw was large enough to swallow even the dragon whole.","Its venom could melt solid stone.","Its scales and hide could effortlessly withstand most attacks.","And despite its enormous bulk, it was remarkably agile.","With all these traits combined, the battle between them was a true clash of equals.","It was a battle between the dragon, the strongest creature on land, and a white serpent that rivaled it.","Their life-or-death struggle showed no sign of ending anytime soon.","Booooom!!!","At last, the white serpent collapsed with more than half its neck torn apart, bringing the long battle to an end.","The fight had lasted for more than half a day.","And the serpent’s neck was far from its only grievous injury.","One of its eyes had been gouged out, and its massive mouth had been ripped apart, leaving its jaw hanging loosely.","Just as the white serpent had opened its maw wide to bite, the dragon had seized the opportunity and shattered its jaw.","\"Grrrrr... Rrrr...\"","But the dragon was hardly in good condition either.","As befitted a battle between evenly matched foes, its body was covered in wounds both large and small.","The most serious injury was to its foreleg.","Its right foreleg had been completely torn off, and blood poured from the stump.","Its wings were no better. They had been shredded so badly that flight was impossible.","But even more dangerous than its wounds was the venom.","The white serpent’s venom was lethal even to a dragon, leaving it in a state where simply enduring was difficult.","\"Grrrr...\"","After checking several times to make sure the white serpent was truly dead, the dragon turned its head.","It looked in the direction of its hatchling—the child for whom it would gladly sacrifice its own life.","But if it tried to travel there now, its strength would fail completely and it would die.","It wanted to rush there immediately, but the dragon suppressed the urge.","Its hatchling was safe.","’...Please.’","The dragon slowly closed its eyes, beginning its recovery in earnest.","No creature could survive in this savage wilderness without the help of its parents.","That was why it had temporarily entrusted its hatchling to Grylls. For reasons it did not understand, the human had protected its child.","If he harmed the hatchling... it would not be too late to take revenge afterward.","Possessing an intellect no less keen than a human’s, the dragon had chosen to gamble on the better odds.","Rustle—","The dragon’s eyes gradually closed.","Its severed foreleg and shredded wing membranes slowly began to regenerate.","It would take at least several days for it to fully recover.","Praying inwardly that its hatchling would remain safe until then, the dragon finally closed its eyes completely.","’Come to think of it, that human...’","Just before its consciousness sank into the depths, the dragon recalled him.","That strangely alien human.","It had no idea why such a human was in this forest.","’Once I wake up, I should speak... with him...’","With that final thought, the dragon’s consciousness faded completely.","And though the dragon had fallen into a deep sleep—","Crack! Craaack!","Its body continued to heal.","***","Day 33 of survival.","I had spent the entire day working, so the hours flew by before I knew it.","In the evening, I also received rice seeds from the Heavenly Demon. Other than that, nothing particularly noteworthy happened.","When I woke up the next morning, I wondered whether Tyranno’s mother had arrived, but no one was there.","Instead, we were greeted by weather that was slightly cooler than before.","\"Kyuuu~ Kyuuu~\"","\"Piiiii! Pii!\"","Even with the cooler weather, the little ones were too busy playing to care.","There was one thing different from yesterday.","A ball.","Wonmo and Tyranno were both having the time of their lives playing with something resembling a soccer ball.","’I tossed it to them just in case, and they’re having a blast.’","Naturally, I had asked Cheonggu Princess for the soccer ball.","She gave me one that looked fairly expensive.","And her condition was incredibly simple: upload a photo or video of the two playing with it.","I had already planned to film them playing anyway.","’But first, I should make them some goalposts.’","I roughly assembled the goalposts out of wood. There was no need to put too much care into making them.","Then I explained the rules to Wonmo and Tyranno.","They were very simple: whoever got the ball between the goalposts scored.","\"Kyuuu!\"","\"Piiiik! Piiik!\"","The two began playing excitedly. I photographed and filmed them just as they were.","The sight alone was enough to fill me with warmth.","Now I was even more curious about how the gallery would react.","Title: Wonmo and Tyranno Are Playing Soccer","Wild Grylls","(A photo of Wonmo enthusiastically kicking the ball)","(A photo of Tyranno enthusiastically kicking the ball)","(A video of Wonmo dribbling the ball and scoring a goal)","(A video of Tyranno slamming his forepaws against the ground in frustration)","Princess Cheonggu, thank you so much for being a princess.","The kids are having a great time thanks to you!","└ Heavenly Demon: Children must grow through play. What a heartwarming sight.","└ SwordMaster: I played a lot of soccer when I was in the army. It’s strange seeing it here.","└ Heavenly Demon: Why would one play soccer in the military? This one cannot understand.","└ SwordMaster: I don’t know either. We just did. Even if it wasn’t soccer, we’d play with anything as long as we had a ball.","└ SwordMaster is right. Knights and soldiers alike will happily play as long as you give them a ball, lmao.","└ Military fact: The older they are, the more insanely good they are at foot volleyball, lmao.","└ In the army, the guys who are good at soccer and foot volleyball are kings;;","└ Suspiciously): Don’t you guys play rugby or American football? We do.","└ They probably play rugby too. But that comes down to preference.","└ And you have to wear armor to play American football;;","└ Just assume they play every ball sport imaginable with vacation days on the line.","└ No one can resist the promise of leave, lmao.","└ Cheonggu Princess: They’re having so much fun! As expected of Chae-U’s future mascot!","└ Who decided he was your mascot?","└ Cheonggu Princess: (Photo of Wonmo wearing a uniform) Can you really say that after seeing this?","└ Lmaoooo, she had that saved.","└ Honestly, he is ridiculously cute, lmao.","└ Put a uniform on Tyranno too.","└ Absolutely not. Tyranno must remain untouched.","└ Aren’t there already teams that use dragons as their symbol?","└ Quite a few countries and territories use dragons as their emblems;;","└ You might get hit with a massive lawsuit if you’re not careful, lmaooo.","└ But can anyone even sue Grylls?","└ No. But Chae-U might get caught in the crossfire, lmaooo.","└ King Leor: Don’t put something filthy on a sacred dragon;; Put our uniform on him instead.","└ Cheonggu Princess: You want him to wear that smelly chicken-head uniform? How horrifying!","└ King Leor: It’s a hawk, not a chicken; are your eyes broken?","└ Cheonggu Princess: I think it’s Coach Leor whose eyes are broken!","└ King Leor: Ffs—","└ Lmaoooooooo.","...!","└ Cheonggu Princess has been roasting King Leor nonstop lately, lmaooo.","└ Understandable. Cheonggu has climbed all the way up to fifth place in the rankings, lmao.","└ PraiseTheSun: Why am I the only one without a dragon? Why am I the only one without a dragon? Why am I the only one without a dragon? Why am I the only one without a dragon?","└ Not having a dragon is normal;","└ He talks like everyone else has one, lmaooo.","└ If every Tom, Dick, and Harry raised a hatchling, the world would’ve ended by now, lmao.","└ I’d rather raise Wonmo than Tyranno.","└ Same. Honestly, I’d choose the gentle-looking Wonmo over the prickly-looking Tyranno, lmao.","└ \"Gentle\": Eats his owner when he gets hungry.","└ Buuurp, lol.","As expected, the response was explosive.","Just reading the comments filled me with satisfaction.","I looked away from the gallery and turned toward Wonmo and Tyranno.","\"Kyuaaaaaak!!!\"","\"Piaaaaaaa!!\"","In the brief moment I had looked away, the two had started fighting.","They were tangled together, rolling around like a ball.","The instant I saw them, I jumped in and barely managed to pull them apart.",".","\"Why are you fighting?! Friends aren’t supposed to fight!\"","\"Kyu! Kyukyukyukyu! Kyukyu!\"","\"Pii! Pipipi! Piiiii!\"","I couldn’t understand a single word.","Judging by how worked up they both were, they must have been furious.","In the end, I summoned Kkobong, our resident animal-language interpreter, and asked her to translate.","First, I heard Wonmo’s side of the story.","\"It was his turn to score. But Tyranno stole the ball.\"","\"And Tyranno?\"","\"If something is taken, it belongs to whoever took it. That is only natural.\"","\"Hmm.\"","So it was because I had explained the rules too vaguely.","After learning what had happened, I carefully admonished them both.","I told them it was my fault for not explaining the rules clearly.","And that if they had a disagreement in the future, they should come to me first.","\"But! Pecking with your beak and biting with your teeth are unacceptable. Neither of you gets any snacks today.\"","\"Kyuuu?!\"","\"Piiiik?!\"","Wonmo and Tyranno both looked utterly horrified when they heard there would be no snacks.","But sometimes a little shock therapy was necessary.","If I spoiled them too much, they might grow up headed in the wrong direction.","\"Keeeng!\"","\"Oh. You’re here?\"","Wonmo and Tyranno were sitting side by side, dejected, when Father Raccoon came to visit me for the first time in a while.","As far as I knew, he had also been busy preparing for winter.","\"What did you find this time?\"","\"Keee...\"","Father Raccoon started to speak, only for his entire body to stiffen.","I had a pretty good idea what he had seen.","Tyranno.","Now that things had turned out this way, it might not be a bad idea to introduce Tyranno to the raccoon family.","\"Oh, right. Let me introduce you. This is Tyranno. As you can see, he’s a baby dragon—a hatchling.\"","\"K-Keeeng...?\"","Father Raccoon looked up at me with an expression that clearly said, A-A dragon?","I gently stroked his head to calm him down.","\"He won’t hurt you, so don’t worry. Didn’t you see the dragon that came here last time?\"","\"Keeeng...\"","\"So you did. That dragon left her baby with me. I don’t know why, though.\"","I finally managed to calm Father Raccoon.","He was still afraid, but his expression was considerably better than before.","Still, I would probably have to take things slowly before introducing Tyranno to his entire family. I still had plenty of other things to do.","At least Father Raccoon could give them a warning in advance.","’I hope the baby raccoons get along with the others.’","That was a matter for later.","For now, I checked what Father Raccoon had brought me.","It was an unusually large seed.","It looked like a coconut at first glance, but it was definitely a seed.","The thing was three times the size of my fist. I could probably grip it and use it as a blunt weapon.","\"What is this? A seed?\"","\"Keeeng!\"","Father Raccoon nodded with a bright smile.","I had no idea what kind of seed it was, but I figured I should plant it.","Father Raccoon had given it to me, so surely nothing strange would sprout from it.","I gave him a Fasting Pill as a reward and headed straight for the garden.","When I arrived, Ludwig was humming as he operated the threshing machine.","Kkobong was working beside him. I had bought her a farmer’s hat because I thought she might be bored, and it suited her surprisingly well.","\"Mister, I’m going to plant this.\"","\"#%%?\"","\"I don’t know what it is. Father Raccoon gave it to me.\"","The seed itself was much larger than my fist, so I would probably have to bury it deeper than usual.","I dug a hole with my shovel and placed the seed inside.","All I had to do was cover it with soil and pour water over it.","Now all that remained was to wait.","Ruuuumble—","\"Huh?\"","Not long after I planted the seed, faint tremors began running through the garden.","Ludwig and Kkobong stopped working and turned toward me.","Even the other animals looked this way.","\"...$%##$?\"","\"I-I don’t know. I just planted it...\"","Ludwig had asked what on earth I had planted, but I couldn’t give him an answer.","Then the garden slowly began to change.","A sprout emerged from the seed.","At first, it was tiny.","Whoooosh!","But the sprout gradually grew until its stalk became almost as thick as a tree trunk.","That alone was enough to tell me this was no ordinary plant.","The real problem, however, was its fruit.","A fruit slowly formed and continued swelling until it became as large as a house.","It was a vivid orange, with a slightly ridged and bumpy surface.","\"A pumpkin?\"","It was a pumpkin.","An absolutely gigantic pumpkin.","They said Cinderella rode to the castle in a pumpkin carriage.","If so, I imagined this was probably the pumpkin she had used.","But the Forest of Four Seasons was far removed from a \"fairy tale.\"","What did I mean by that?","Creeeak—","The center of the pumpkin slowly split open, revealing rows of razor-sharp teeth like those of a shark.","Then eyes and a nose appeared as well, making it look even more threatening.","\"Kyaaaaaaaa!!!\"","This wasn’t a fairy tale.","It was Halloween.","’What the hell did he give me...?’","I would think about that after I caught it."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204","paragraphs":["Jack-o’-Lantern (1)","The pumpkin monster known as the jack-o’-lantern could be considered the symbol of Halloween.","Its distinguishing features were its sharply carved mouth and the hollow openings that served as its eyes and nose.","And as the word \"lantern\" suggested, its interior was empty but filled with light.","From what I knew, jack-o’-lanterns rarely harmed people and generally limited themselves to playing pranks.","\"Kyaaaa! Kyaaaaaaa!\"","\"What the hell is this?\"","But that only applied when they were small.","The pumpkin head before me was as large as a house.","It looked threatening enough to swallow a person whole in a single bite.","The same went for its shriek. It sounded exactly like something a monster would make.","It certainly suited a fantasy world, but I was more worried than impressed.","’How am I supposed to kill something like this...?’","Unlike a beast, this thing was a plant. It had no obvious vital points.","There was fire, widely regarded as the natural enemy of all plants, but the question was whether it would work on this creature.","There was something else that bothered me as well.","’Father Raccoon wouldn’t have given me something dangerous...’","Until now, Father Raccoon had always brought me highly effective medicinal herbs or mushrooms.","That was why I had planted the seed he brought this time without much suspicion.","Yet the moment I planted it, some kind of pumpkin monster appeared.","I couldn’t help wondering whether it merely looked frightening and was actually friendly.","Thump!","Just as that thought crossed my mind, the jack-o’-lantern astonishingly launched itself high into the air.","I wondered how something that enormous could possibly jump so high, but I didn’t have long to think about it.","\"Fwooooop!\"","The jack-o’-lantern tilted its head backward.","\"Tutututututu!!!\"","Then it fired something from its mouth.","The projectiles were moving incredibly fast.","They weren’t too fast for me to dodge after seeing them, so I predicted their trajectories and evaded.","Papapapapak!","\"Kyuuu!\"","\"Piiiik!\"","The other animals hurriedly scattered as well.","I checked to see what the creature had spat out.","\"S-Seeds...?\"","The things fired by the jack-o’-lantern were none other than seeds.","They were enormous, comparable in size to the one I had planted.","But that wasn’t the end of it.","Rustle... Rustle...","The seeds began burrowing into the ground by themselves.","Horrified by the sight, I urgently shouted.","\"K-Kkobong! Pull those out, quickly! Hurry!\"","\"Understood!\"","\"Wonmo and Tyranno, you two help too! We’ll be in serious trouble if those things get underground!\"","\"Kyuuu!\"","\"Piiiii!\"","At my urgent command, my animal companions hurriedly removed the seeds as they burrowed into the soil.","Fortunately, the seeds sank into the ground rather slowly, so we barely managed to remove every last one.","Thud!","The jack-o’-lantern, however, remained perfectly fine.","Its massive body... Could I even call it a body?","Either way, the pumpkin came crashing back down.","Whoosh!","At that moment, Ludwig charged toward the jack-o’-lantern.","He was holding the Mithricon sword, though I had no idea when he had drawn it.","Apparently, he had been preparing to attack while the animals and I removed the seeds.","Shhhhh—","A green galaxy began flowing across the Mithricon sword in his hand.","At the same time, sharp aura formed around the entire weapon as if coating it.","Aura Blade.","It was a technique he had shown me several times before.","With the Mithricon sword and Aura Blade working together, it should be capable of cutting through steel with ease.","Shashashashak!","Ludwig appeared to swing his sword only once, yet dozens of slashes followed.","They were so fast that even my dynamic vision could barely track them.","He shouldn’t have been able to properly circulate the mana within his body, yet he could still move that quickly.","Just how strong had this man been outside the forest?","I grew more curious by the moment.","Thud! Thump!","Under Ludwig’s concise and efficient assault, the jack-o’-lantern was cleanly sliced into pieces.","It had been as large as a house, yet a few swings of his sword had killed it with absurd ease.","I was about to relax, thinking it was over.","Float—","The pumpkin fragments Ludwig had cut apart rose into the air.","Shhk! Shashak! Shak!","Then they began returning to their original positions.","Both Ludwig and I stared at them with our eyes wide open.","The moment all the pieces fused back together, the jack-o’-lantern’s distinctive expression reappeared on the pumpkin.","\"Kyaaaaaaa!!!\"","Ludwig retreated in bewilderment at the jack-o’-lantern’s shriek.","I was just as dumbfounded.","I had clearly seen inside it when Ludwig cut it to pieces.","’It was just an ordinary pumpkin.’","There had been nothing inside it other than a handful of seeds.","I hadn’t seen anything that could be called an inner core or nucleus.","Then how had the jack-o’-lantern regenerated?","Thump!","While I pondered the question, the jack-o’-lantern launched itself high into the air again.","Was it going to repeat the same attack?","I was about to raise my shield in preparation when—","Crack!","\"Fwooooop...! Gwehk!\"","Something struck the jack-o’-lantern as it tilted its head back, sending it plummeting to the ground.","I didn’t know what had hit it, but it had been shot down.","I turned my head, searching for the cause.","\"Ggueong.\"","It didn’t take me long to find it.","Largo had a brick clamped between his jaws.","Apparently, he had swung his long neck and hurled the brick like a catapult.","He was a literal living catapult.","Thanks to him, I had been spared quite a bit of trouble.","\"Thuuud!\"","The jack-o’-lantern crashed to the ground upside down.","We couldn’t afford to let this opportunity slip away.","Ludwig and I both rushed toward the fallen jack-o’-lantern without needing to say a word.","The creature was too busy trying to right itself.","It seemed to have difficulty controlling its body because of its enormous size.","Shashashashak! Shashashashashak!","Ludwig launched the first attack.","Just as before, the jack-o’-lantern was sliced into countless pieces.","Then it was my turn to finish it.","I enlarged my aura to an enormous size and brought it crashing down on the fragments.","Rather than trying to cut them, I struck with the intention of crushing them completely.","Booom! Bang! Bang!","The shattered chunks of pumpkin were reduced to pulp.","It was a waste, but there was nothing else I could do.","I had to deal with the immediate danger first.","And so, the jack-o’-lantern was not merely torn to pieces, but mashed into pulp.","At this point, surely it couldn’t regenerate again.","I muttered quietly.","\"...Did we get it?\"","\"You stupid bastard!\"","The moment I said that, Ludwig roared at me.","Startled by his sudden outburst, I turned toward him.","He was staring at me as if I had just uttered a forbidden phrase.","Only then did I realize what a terrible mistake I had made.","Float... Float...","And the consequences were catastrophic.","The jack-o’-lantern, which had been not only torn apart but mashed into pulp, was slowly regenerating.","Why the hell could it regenerate?","If it had been an animal, I might have understood.","There had been the case of the saber-toothed tiger—an individual whose regenerative abilities had been enhanced by possessing a heart comparable to a Dragon Heart.","But this creature wasn’t an animal. It was a plant.","Nor was there anywhere it could be absorbing nutrients from.","’Could it be the soil? No, that can’t be it. It doesn’t have any roots—’","The moment I remembered that the jack-o’-lantern had no \"roots,\" my mind snapped into focus.","It felt as though a bolt of lightning had flashed through my head.","I immediately turned around.","My gaze landed directly on the garden.","The garden where this creature had grown.","It was a theory that completely defied conventional wisdom, but this was a fantasy world.","More than that, this was the Forest of Four Seasons, a place where even the common sense of a fantasy world didn’t apply.","Rather than thinking logically, it might be better to follow my instincts.","\"Mister! Keep that bastard occupied!\"","\"Where are you going?\"","\"I just thought of something! And everyone, stay behind me just in case!\"","Immediately after giving the order, I picked up a shovel instead of my sword and shield.","I began digging in the part of the garden where I had planted the jack-o’-lantern.","And then—","\"Found it!\"","It didn’t take long for me to uncover the jack-o’-lantern’s \"roots.\"","I had no idea how it worked, but the roots were continuously supplying nutrients to the distant pumpkin.","’Does this world have Bluetooth roots too?’","At this rate, I wouldn’t be surprised if a Bluetooth showerhead appeared next.","Casting aside that useless thought, I grabbed the rhizome with all my strength.","Rustle!","Plants had wills of their own.","And this one was a monster.","The instant I seized its roots, vines burst out and frantically tried to bind my body.","One of them initially aimed for my neck, but I narrowly dodged it.","\"Hey! Kkobong! Grab this!\"","\"Uoh!\"","\"You guys grab one each too!\"","I gave instructions to Kkobong and the rest of my animal companions.","Once they had each seized a root or vine with their hands or mouths, I shouted with all my strength.","\"Puuuuull!\"","\"Kyuuuuuu!\"","\"Piiiiiiik!\"","I didn’t know whether the roots had burrowed extraordinarily deep or were simply resisting with all their might.","Even with one human and four animals pulling together, they showed no sign of coming free.","Behind us, Ludwig was keeping the giant pumpkin head at bay, but I had no idea how long he could hold out.","Rustle!","\"Kegh!\"","To make matters worse, one vine was still free.","Perhaps it had realized that I was the key figure, because it wrapped itself around my neck.","The pressure on my throat steadily increased, and my vision gradually began to blur.","But I refused to give up.","Through the roots in my hands, I could feel the other animals continuing to pull without surrendering.","If we failed to uproot this thing, there was no telling what else it might try.","Crack!","The fruits of our effort gradually began to show.","The distinctive sensation of roots being pulled free traveled through my hands.","I could vividly feel the creature struggling desperately to remain buried, but it was already too late.","The soil had already released its grip on the roots.","Even as the vine strangled me, I shouted.","\"Kegh! Now! Pull!\"","\"Uoooooh!!!\"","Crack-crack-crack-crack!","When we suddenly put more strength into it, the roots finally began emerging from the ground.","At the same time, the pressure around my neck grew even stronger.","But it was already too late.","Before long, the entire root system had been dragged out of the soil.","Craaaack! Pop!","We had finally uprooted the absurdly tenacious roots of the jack-o’-lantern.","They writhed as if they were alive, but the roots themselves were even more astonishing.","\"Kieeeeeee!\"","That wasn’t a root.","It was a miniature jack-o’-lantern.","And it was radiating a brilliant light.","Was it some kind of arrangement where the little one controlled the enormous one?","Whatever the case, we had found its weakness.","All that remained was to finish the job.","Thwack!","\"Kuehk!\"","When I punched the jack-o’-lantern hanging beneath the roots, it shrieked.","Apparently, it could feel pain.","It was similar to a fully grown mandrake.","That made things much easier.","I spoke to Kkobong.","\"Kkobong! Beat the crap out of this bastard!\"","\"Uoh!\"","Kkobong was far more proficient in martial arts than I was.","What did that mean?","Thudududududu!","\"Gguehk! Ggueeek! Ggueeeeeek!\"","It meant she pounded the creature like a punching bag.","As though venting all the stress that had accumulated until now, Kkobong gleefully pummeled it.","The more Kkobong struck it, the weaker the vine constricting my neck became.","The same was true of the giant pumpkin head Ludwig was fighting.","With its main body under attack, it could do nothing but twitch and was unable to move properly.","Limp—","After enduring a spectacular barrage of punches from Kkobong, the entire root system went limp.","The creature’s screams also died away.","It seemed to have lost consciousness.","When I looked at its face, its mouth, nose, and eyes had all vanished as though they had never existed.","Deciding that was enough, I was just about to tell Kkobong to stop when—","\"Bleurgh.\"","Something dropped out of the giant jack-o’-lantern’s mouth.","It was an orb radiating an orange glow.","Anyone could tell at a glance that it resembled an inner core.","However, it was rather large—about half the size of my fist.","If I tried swallowing it whole, it would get stuck in my throat.","\"The inner core is one thing, but I wonder if this is useful too.\"","I looked at the jack-o’-lantern’s main body.","I had no idea whether I could use it.","Now that it had expelled its inner core, it might have reverted to an ordinary pumpkin.","Even so, there was a high probability that it contained energy comparable to the inner core.","The fish had been the same.","Creatures that possessed inner cores were usually precious in their entirety.","\"#%@^?\"","Once the situation had settled down, Ludwig walked over and spoke to me.","He pointed somewhere, so I turned my head in that direction.","With the miniature main body incapacitated, the giant pumpkin head had become an ordinary pumpkin.","It was still just as enormous, though.","What could we possibly do with it?","\"We’ll eat it, I guess.\"","\"Eat it?\"","\"Yes.\"","Pumpkins had long been considered a winter delicacy.","\"Should we steam some pumpkin later?\"","Our food supply had just become even more abundant."]}]);
